**4.1.2 Multinomial Coefficients**

## I Definitions

A. (_n_; \(n\), \(n\)2, . . . , \(n\),_n_) is the number of ways of putting \(n\) = \(n\)1+_n_2+ . . . + \(n\) different objects into \(m\) different boxes with \(n\)1 in the _k_-th box, _k = 1_, 2_, . . ., \(m\).

(_n_; \(a\)1, \(a\)2, . . . , _a_)* is the number of permutations of \(n\) = \(a\)1+ 2\(a\)2+ . . . + _na_ symbols composed of \(a\)1 cycles of length \(k\) for \(k\) = 1, 2, . . . , \(n\).

(_n_; \(a\)1, \(a\)2, . . . , _a_)' is the number of ways of partitioning a set of \(n\) = \(a\)1+ 2\(a\)2+ . . . + _na_* different objects into \(a\)1 subsets containing \(k\) objects for \(k\) = 1, 2, . . ., \(n\).

